course: dictionary
lesson: 2143
title: Tiny drifting animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A copepod is a tiny animal with a hard shell and many legs. It is a relative of crabs and shrimps, and it lives in the sea and in fresh water.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. «Plankton are tiny drifting living things, such as algae, baby fish and copepods.» Copepods are named in a list of tiny living things, so they must be small too.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "tiny animal with a hard shell" in place of copepod, and the sentence still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A copepod is a tiny animal with a hard shell and many legs.
fact: Copepods are relatives of crabs and shrimps.
fact: Copepods live in the sea and in fresh water.
fact: Copepods are part of plankton, the tiny drifting living things in the ocean.
fact: Some copepods are smaller than a grain of rice, and there are many thousands of kinds.
exercise: «Plankton are tiny drifting living things, such as algae, baby fish and copepods.» What is a copepod? | A large fish that swims in rivers | A kind of bird that lives on cliffs | A tall plant that grows on the seabed | *A tiny animal with a hard shell and many legs
exercise: Copepods are relatives of which animals? | Snakes and lizards | Frogs and toads | Trees and bushes | *Crabs and shrimps
exercise: Where do copepods live? | *In the sea and in fresh water | Only in the sea, never in fresh water | Only at the tops of mountains | Only on land, in deserts
test: Some copepods are smaller than what? | *A grain of rice | A football | A cat | A pencil
test: Copepods are part of which group of tiny living things? | Fossils | Crowds | *Plankton | Shells
exam: What kind of word is copepod? | An adjective, meaning tiny | *A noun, a name for a thing | A verb, meaning to swim | An adverb, meaning slowly
